  "summary": "Commercial illustration style featuring idealized Mexican women and cultural motifs used in advertising and calendars.",
  "description": "Characterized by stylized depictions of Mexican women with European facial features and indigenous clothing elements, surrounded by decorative patterns and text. Developed by commercial artists like Posada and Covarrubias, blending European pin-up aesthetics with Mexican cultural symbols to create a distinctive advertising style that became popular throughout Latin America.",
